=== About Me

I am a postdoctoral researcher in the Department of Engineering Science, University of Oxford, U.K. My advisor is Prof. [https://sysos.eng.ox.ac.uk/our-group/antonis-papachristodoulou/ Antonis Papachristodoulou]. I obtained PhD under the supervision of Prof. [https://www.deschutter.info/ Bart De Schutter], Prof. [https://www.tudelft.nl/en/staff/a.j.j.vandenboom/?cHash=e29f8ef4a6d74d32f988c13324671cf8/ Ton van den Boom], and Dr. [https://www.tudelft.nl/staff/s.shi-3/ Shengling Shi] at the [https://www.tudelft.nl/3me/over/afdelingen/delft-center-for-systems-and-control/ Delft Center for Systems and Control], Delft University of Technology, the Netherlands. I received the B.S. degree in the School of Mechanical Engineering and Automation, [http://ev.buaa.edu.cn/ Beihang University] (BUAA), in 2018, and the M.S. degree (with an outstanding graduation thesis and Chinese national scholarship) in the Department of Dynamics and Control, Beihang University, in 2021. I was a research assistant in the group of [https://www.au.tsinghua.edu.cn/info/1081/3094.htm/ Dr. Zhang Chen], in the [https://www.au.tsinghua.edu.cn/ Department of Automation], Tsinghua University, China, in 2021.

My Postdoc research: [https://www.nwo.nl/en/projects/rkcdr01201/ Integrated Learning and Optimisation for Safety-Critical Control] is funded by the [https://www.nwo.nl/en/researchprogrammes/rubicon/ Rubicon Fellowship, NWO]. My PhD research topic is about learning-based control under constraints, which is a part of an ERC Advanced Project "A novel control paradigm for large-scale hybrid networks" ([https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/101018826/ CLariNet]).

=== Research Interests

My main interests involve developing learning-based control methods with safety guarantees and computational efficiency, and their applications in mobile robots. I use tools from control theory (model predictive control, control barrier functions), optimization (mixed-integer programming, parametric programming, stochastic programming), and machine learning (reinforcement learning, Gaussian process).

=== Master 

I am actively looking for supervision of master's thesis projects at the University of Oxford (can be remote). Please see the [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VKvVwAtupN0v70RYK-wdrLpyxNEmkC1c/view?usp=sharing/ description of master's projects]. Feel free to contact me if you are interested. The topics include 

- generative policies for robot planning
- integrated RL and MPC for vehicle–traffic coordination
- machine learning for speeding up mixed-integer optimization with applications in multi-contact robots
- Safe learning and control in latent-space world Models,

=== Recent News
~~~
- *Feb. 2025* I will go to KU Leuven for a short research visit, where I will address safety reinforcement learning with probabilistic guarantees with Prof. [https://www.esat.kuleuven.be/sista/members/suykens.html/ Johan Suykens].

- *Dec. 2024* I present at IEEE CDC 2024 on our paper "Efficient and safe learning-based control of piecewise affine systems using optimization-free safety filters".

- *Oct 2024* My recent work "Approximate dynamic programming for constrained piecewise affine systems with stability and safety guarantees" was accepted by IEEE Transactions on Systems, Man, and Cybernetics: Systems.

- *Nov. 2023* I propose a [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1feGRN3VqMDWLniLTGDhUgQsZmAorAl-b/view?usp=drive_link/ master project] on safe reinforcement learning for autonomous driving. Please contact me if you are searching for a master project.

- *Oct. 2023* My recent work "Approximate dynamic programming for constrained linear systems: a piecewise quadratic approximation approach" was accepted by Automatica 
